From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Connor Prussin <connor@prussin.net>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: an agent's copies in a page stay on its own
 clipboard

A page an agent's input last drove copies to and pastes from that agent
seat's own clipboard, never the desktop's, which the compositor puts on
the user's seat. //chrome/browser/domicile/domicile_agent_input.cc
chooses it (components/domicile/browser/agent_clipboards.h). What it
needs of //ui and //content:

- ui::ScopedClipboardRedirect: while one lives, the thread's
  Clipboard::GetForCurrentThread() answers another clipboard. A
  ScopedClipboardWriter commits to whatever that answers.
- ClipboardNonBacked::CreateDomicileSeparate(): an in-memory clipboard
  beside the thread's, for an agent.
- ClipboardHostImpl::Context::GetClipboard(): the clipboard a context
  reads, its writer commits to and its paste source comes from. A
  frame's asks //chrome (content/public/browser/domicile_clipboard.h).
